      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KRAKEY (7) has been competitive of late and kept the ball rolling last time when 9 metres from the winner in fifth over 2190m at Shepparton. The driver has some work to do from this wide starting position. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. GLENLINE (8) won at Ballarat two runs ago before finishing an unlucky fourth at his latest appearance over 1690m at this track, beaten 6 metres after getting denied racing room in the run home. Can travel in a nice spot from this draw and wait on the sprint lane if necessary. Won't find this any harder and he can finish a lot closer this time. TEX GOES BANG (6) veteran who didn't do a bad job when sixth over 2080m at Cranbourne last time out after racing outside the leader at the bell. Include in in exotic bets. DOT BALL (4) is worth some thought despite her last-start seventh over 1690m at this track on October 22.",
